ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

py_m_map is an independent Python re-implementation of the m_map mapping
toolbox for MATLAB by Rich Pawlowicz (Department of Earth, Ocean and
Atmospheric Sciences, University of British Columbia),
https://www-old.eoas.ubc.ca/~rich/map.html

The API, function names and figure conventions deliberately follow m_map so that
existing m_map users and course material carry across. No m_map source code or
data files are included or redistributed here; the implementation was written
independently against m_map's documented behaviour. If you use py_m_map in
published work, please credit m_map as the origin of the design.

Bundled data:

  py_m_map/data/topo_1deg.npz
      1-degree global topography, produced by block-averaging ETOPO1
      (ice-surface, grid-registered) to one degree.

      ETOPO1 source: Amante, C. and B. W. Eakins, 2009. ETOPO1 1 Arc-Minute
      Global Relief Model: Procedures, Data Sources and Analysis. NOAA
      Technical Memorandum NESDIS NGDC-24. National Geophysical Data Center,
      NOAA. doi:10.7289/V5C8276M

      As a work of the United States Government, ETOPO1 is not subject to
      domestic copyright protection.
